WEBVTT

1
00:00:30.125 --> 00:00:36.958
<b>In this verse, Lord Krishna is explaining the </b>
<b>difference between the ignorant and the wise.</b>

2
00:00:36.958 --> 00:00:39.250
<b>He tells Arjuna,</b>

3
00:00:39.250 --> 00:00:41.625
<b>"O descendant of Bharata, Arjuna,</b>

4
00:00:41.625 --> 00:00:47.500
<b>where an ignorant person performs </b>
<b>actions with attachment to the results,</b>

5
00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:53.708
<b>the wise person is one whose process</b>
<b>of action may be the same,</b>

6
00:00:53.708 --> 00:00:57.000
<b>but they have no attachment to the outcome.</b>

7
00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:59.708
<b>Their goals are not personal;</b>

8
00:00:59.708 --> 00:01:07.791
<b>they act only for the welfare of society or </b>
<b>to guide others on the right path."</b>

9
00:01:12.458 --> 00:01:13.875
<b>In the first chapter,</b>

10
00:01:13.875 --> 00:01:16.333
<b>Arjuna Vishada Yoga, we learned</b>

11
00:01:16.333 --> 00:01:19.125
<b>that Arjuna was worried about the </b>
<b>bondage of karma</b>

12
00:01:19.125 --> 00:01:22.333
<b>or the sin and merit associated with his actions.</b>

13
00:01:22.333 --> 00:01:25.750
<b>It is possible that a question arises</b>
<b>in Arjuna's mind here: </b>

14
00:01:25.750 --> 00:01:29.208
<b>"Let's assume that we perform </b>
<b>actions not for personal gain</b>

15
00:01:29.208 --> 00:01:35.916
<b>but to guide others. </b>
<b>Still, the action has been performed,</b>

16
00:01:35.916 --> 00:01:39.208
<b>and if the action is done, there will also </b>
<b>be the bondage of karma,</b>

17
00:01:39.208 --> 00:01:43.541
<b>and there will be sin and </b>
<b>merit related to this action."</b>

18
00:01:43.541 --> 00:01:48.458
<b>This is where we need to understand </b>
<b>Lord Krishna's words deeply.</b>

19
00:01:48.458 --> 00:01:57.541
<b>Where an ignorant person acts in this life and </b>
<b>even in heaven after life only to obtain pleasure, </b>

20
00:01:57.541 --> 00:01:58.916
<b>they are attached;</b>

21
00:01:58.916 --> 00:02:02.916
<b>their goal is personal, not spiritual.</b>

22
00:02:02.916 --> 00:02:09.041
<b>On the other hand, when a wise person acts, </b>
<b>their goal is not personal.</b>

23
00:02:09.041 --> 00:02:11.916
<b>Here, the actions of both may be the same,</b>

24
00:02:11.916 --> 00:02:13.958
<b>but the difference lies in the goal.</b>

25
00:02:13.958 --> 00:02:19.250
<b>It also differs in the consciousness of </b>
<b>why that action is being performed.</b>

26
00:02:19.250 --> 00:02:21.875
<b>And this very consciousness determines</b>

27
00:02:21.875 --> 00:02:27.541
<b>whether a person will remain bound by</b>
<b>the karmic bonds of sin and merit or not.</b>

28
00:02:27.541 --> 00:02:31.416
<b>why take on the dilemmas </b>
<b>associated with action?</b>

29
00:02:31.416 --> 00:02:37.750
<b>then indirectly, this is also a personal </b>
<b>desire for a comfortable life.</b>

30
00:02:37.750 --> 00:02:40.333
<b>Therefore, there is no escape from action.</b>

31
00:02:40.333 --> 00:02:43.458
<b>Lord Krishna Himself, despite being God,</b>

32
00:02:43.458 --> 00:02:47.291
<b>is performing actions in this form on earth.</b>

33
00:02:47.291 --> 00:02:48.166
<b>Thus,</b>

34
00:02:48.166 --> 00:02:50.958
<b>the path of action is the right path,</b>

35
00:02:50.958 --> 00:02:54.500
<b>and the difference between the ignorant </b>
<b>and the wise is only this: </b>

36
00:02:54.500 --> 00:02:58.958
<b>where one person acts in pursuit of personal fruit,</b>

37
00:02:58.958 --> 00:03:04.166
<b>the other does it as a duty, without attachment.</b>

38
00:03:04.166 --> 00:03:10.375
<b>In the end, spiritual progress is made by </b>
<b>the one who is free from karmic bondage,</b>

39
00:03:10.375 --> 00:03:15.291
<b>who has renounced attachments </b>
<b>or concerns about results.</b>

40
00:03:19.833 --> 00:03:22.375
<b>In our personal lives,</b>

41
00:03:22.375 --> 00:03:30.541
<b>we usually perform any action </b>
<b>expecting a good result.</b>

42
00:03:30.541 --> 00:03:35.625
<b>We work hard at the workplace </b>
<b>for professional growth,</b>

43
00:03:35.625 --> 00:03:38.625
<b>earn money for a big car</b>

44
00:03:38.625 --> 00:03:40.750
<b>or a big house.</b>

45
00:03:40.750 --> 00:03:43.125
<b>These are big examples;</b>

46
00:03:43.125 --> 00:03:49.458
<b>let's take a small task like</b>
<b>cooking a meal for guests.</b>

47
00:03:49.458 --> 00:03:54.125
<b>Even here, there is an expectation of the outcome</b>

48
00:03:54.125 --> 00:04:00.666
<b>that the guests will like the food and praise it.</b>

49
00:04:00.666 --> 00:04:02.458
<b>Right?</b>

50
00:04:02.458 --> 00:04:04.666
<b>After doing any work,</b>

51
00:04:04.666 --> 00:04:13.000
<b>the thought of what fruit will be obtained </b>
<b>keeps going along with the work.</b>

52
00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:18.916
<b>Now someone might ask, what's wrong with that?</b>

53
00:04:18.916 --> 00:04:21.250
<b>Think about it,</b>

54
00:04:21.250 --> 00:04:23.791
<b>will thinking about the result,</b>

55
00:04:23.791 --> 00:04:25.958
<b>worrying about it,</b>

56
00:04:25.958 --> 00:04:29.458
<b>change the result?</b>

57
00:04:29.458 --> 00:04:30.750
<b>No, right?</b>

58
00:04:30.750 --> 00:04:33.291
<b>Yes, it is possible</b>

59
00:04:33.291 --> 00:04:38.500
<b>that the constant worry about the </b>
<b>result may hinder your work,</b>

60
00:04:38.500 --> 00:04:44.208
<b>which may ultimately have an </b>
<b>adverse effect on the result itself.</b>

61
00:04:44.208 --> 00:04:47.041
<b>Understand this with an example,</b>

62
00:04:47.041 --> 00:04:50.708
<b>A student is practicing for an exam.</b>

63
00:04:50.708 --> 00:04:56.666
<b>What will happen if the worry about the </b>
<b>result starts to haunt them too much?</b>

64
00:04:56.666 --> 00:05:00.666
<b>This worry can definitely increase mental stress,</b>

65
00:05:00.666 --> 00:05:05.666
<b>which will adversely affect the student's practice.</b>

66
00:05:05.666 --> 00:05:07.416
<b>And ultimately,</b>

67
00:05:07.416 --> 00:05:10.125
<b>if the practice is not done well,</b>

68
00:05:10.125 --> 00:05:17.041
<b> you can imagine for yourself what </b>
<b>effect it will have on the result. </b>

69
00:05:17.041 --> 00:05:18.625
<b>You tell me,</b>

70
00:05:18.625 --> 00:05:20.125
<b>what would be better?</b>

71
00:05:20.125 --> 00:05:23.708
<b>To practice with constant worry about the result?</b>

72
00:05:23.708 --> 00:05:27.375
<b>Or to give up the worry of the result</b>

73
00:05:27.375 --> 00:05:33.541
<b>and focus all your attention only </b>
<b>on studying and practicing?</b>

74
00:05:33.541 --> 00:05:38.375
<b>Your life is no different from this.</b>

75
00:05:38.375 --> 00:05:40.125
<b>Will worrying about the result</b>

76
00:05:40.125 --> 00:05:47.541
<b>or being anxious about the </b>
<b>future change the result or the future?</b>

77
00:05:47.541 --> 00:05:49.000
<b>No, right?</b>

78
00:05:49.000 --> 00:05:53.666
<b>The future and the result will change</b>

79
00:05:53.666 --> 00:06:01.166
<b>only when your present is </b>
<b>solely dedicated to your actions.</b>

80
00:06:01.166 --> 00:06:03.625
<b>Think about this</b>

81
00:06:03.625 --> 00:06:08.041
<b>and also apply it in life.</b>

82
00:06:08.041 --> 00:06:09.333
<b>Yes,</b>

83
00:06:09.333 --> 00:06:16.500
<b>it sounds easy to hear but difficult to do.</b>

84
00:06:16.500 --> 00:06:17.958
<b>For this,</b>

85
00:06:17.958 --> 00:06:19.208
<b>meditation,</b>

86
00:06:19.208 --> 00:06:21.000
<b>spirituality,</b>

87
00:06:21.000 --> 00:06:22.708
<b>this Gita,</b>

88
00:06:22.708 --> 00:06:25.458
<b>all these will be your helpers.</b>

89
00:06:25.458 --> 00:06:32.291
<b>Keep them with you and</b>
<b>focus only on your actions.</b>

90
00:06:36.958 --> 00:06:41.708
<b>In this verse, I spoke to Arjuna </b>
<b>about two types of people:</b>

91
00:06:41.708 --> 00:06:45.125
<b>those who are not attached to the results,</b>

92
00:06:45.125 --> 00:06:50.458
<b>and others who are constantly</b>
<b>attached to the results. </b>

93
00:06:50.458 --> 00:06:52.125
<b>In both situations, </b>

94
00:06:52.125 --> 00:06:56.208
<b>the effects of these people </b>
<b>are not limited to them alone</b>

95
00:06:56.208 --> 00:07:01.833
<b>but also definitely fall on other </b>
<b>people in the community or family.</b>

96
00:07:01.833 --> 00:07:03.625
<b>For example,</b>

97
00:07:03.625 --> 00:07:08.875
<b>if either the father or the mother </b>
<b>is constantly worried,</b>

98
00:07:08.875 --> 00:07:12.958
<b>it will also affect the children.</b>

99
00:07:12.958 --> 00:07:17.416
<b>Let's say a father is always worried about his job,</b>

100
00:07:17.416 --> 00:07:23.750
<b>or he does every task only and only for profit,</b>

101
00:07:23.750 --> 00:07:28.500
<b>even if he has to exploit others for it.</b>

102
00:07:28.500 --> 00:07:36.416
<b>That father may believe that he is </b>
<b>doing all this to support his family,</b>

103
00:07:36.416 --> 00:07:38.333
<b>but this worry,</b>

104
00:07:38.333 --> 00:07:41.791
<b>this stress, exploiting others for success.</b>

105
00:07:41.791 --> 00:07:44.791
<b>What effect will it have on the children?</b>

106
00:07:44.791 --> 00:07:48.916
<b>The children will learn what they see, right?</b>

107
00:07:48.916 --> 00:07:53.583
<b>They will start believing that being so worried,</b>

108
00:07:53.583 --> 00:07:57.125
<b>not caring about others for the sake of profit,</b>

109
00:07:57.125 --> 00:07:59.500
<b>is the truth of life.</b>

110
00:07:59.500 --> 00:08:01.083
<b>On the other hand,</b>

111
00:08:01.083 --> 00:08:06.791
<b>if another father performs </b>
<b>all his duties with focus.</b>

112
00:08:06.791 --> 00:08:10.083
<b>When at work, he works;</b>

113
00:08:10.083 --> 00:08:15.291
<b>when he comes home, he spends </b>
<b>loving time with his family,</b>

114
00:08:15.291 --> 00:08:19.125
<b>helps his children with their studies.</b>

115
00:08:19.125 --> 00:08:20.375
<b>And he</b>

116
00:08:20.375 --> 00:08:23.166
<b>does all these tasks leaving behind </b>
<b>the worries of the future,</b>

117
00:08:23.166 --> 00:08:28.708
<b>living in that one moment of the present, </b>
<b>with full concentration.</b>

118
00:08:28.708 --> 00:08:32.666
<b>This positive influence will also be on the children.</b>

119
00:08:32.666 --> 00:08:35.916
<b>They will know the value of family affection,</b>

120
00:08:35.916 --> 00:08:39.916
<b>the importance of being cheerful, </b>
<b>the benefits of focus.</b>

121
00:08:39.916 --> 00:08:44.416
<b>And this will make their life easier going forward.</b>

122
00:08:44.416 --> 00:08:47.750
<b>In the family, elders have to </b>
<b>set an example themselves.</b>

123
00:08:47.750 --> 00:08:54.000
<b>Fulfilling duties, doing every task with focus,</b>
<b>not worrying about the future,</b>

124
00:08:54.000 --> 00:08:56.333
<b>and thinking about the welfare of others, </b>

125
00:08:56.333 --> 00:09:01.166
<b>all these life values have to be </b>
<b>adopted by the elders themselves.</b>

126
00:09:01.166 --> 00:09:05.333
<b>Only then will it have a positive </b>
<b>effect on the next generation.</b>

127
00:09:05.333 --> 00:09:08.041
<b>This will create a foundation of society</b>

128
00:09:08.041 --> 00:09:11.166
<b>where there is cooperation, trust,</b>

129
00:09:11.166 --> 00:09:13.416
<b> and love.</b>

130
00:09:18.041 --> 00:09:23.583
<b>In professional life, we often tie our </b>
<b>happiness, our self-respect,</b>

131
00:09:23.583 --> 00:09:28.333
<b>only and only with the results.</b>

132
00:09:28.333 --> 00:09:30.500
<b>Is this appropriate?</b>

133
00:09:30.500 --> 00:09:33.916
<b>Of course, the question will arise in the mind,</b>

134
00:09:33.916 --> 00:09:36.875
<b>should the thought of results be abandoned then?</b>

135
00:09:36.875 --> 00:09:40.000
<b>Should ambitions be forgotten?</b>

136
00:09:40.000 --> 00:09:42.375
<b>Understand the essence of this...</b>

137
00:09:42.375 --> 00:09:46.333
<b>Not worrying about the </b>
<b>result does not mean at all</b>

138
00:09:46.333 --> 00:09:49.041
<b>that you have given up your ambitions.</b>

139
00:09:49.041 --> 00:09:51.916
<b>Understand it this way,</b>

140
00:09:51.916 --> 00:09:59.541
<b>that you plan with focus, you work hard </b>
<b>with focus, you solve problems with focus.</b>

141
00:09:59.541 --> 00:10:04.541
<b>Probably this is why the result </b>
<b>will be good in such a case.</b>

142
00:10:04.541 --> 00:10:07.250
<b>But what if the result was the opposite?</b>

143
00:10:07.250 --> 00:10:08.958
<b>Even then?</b>

144
00:10:08.958 --> 00:10:11.708
<b>Would it be right to be sadabout </b>
<b>the adverse result?</b>

145
00:10:11.708 --> 00:10:16.250
<b>Would it be right to doubt your </b>
<b>abilities based on that adverse result?</b>

146
00:10:16.250 --> 00:10:22.125
<b>Or would it be right that whatever the result, </b>
<b>without being distressed by it,</b>

147
00:10:22.125 --> 00:10:26.833
<b>you once again start planning, </b>
<b>start working hard.</b>

148
00:10:26.833 --> 00:10:30.625
<b>If your focus was only on your actions.</b>

149
00:10:30.625 --> 00:10:39.500
<b>That is, if your focus was only on your planning, </b>
<b>your hard work, solving problems,</b>

150
00:10:39.500 --> 00:10:41.250
<b>then ultimately</b>

151
00:10:41.250 --> 00:10:43.791
<b>the result will definitely be beautiful.</b>

152
00:10:43.791 --> 00:10:46.083
<b>Results do not improve by worrying,</b>

153
00:10:46.083 --> 00:10:50.125
<b>nor do they improve by dreaming beautiful </b>
<b>dreams about them.</b>

154
00:10:50.125 --> 00:10:58.041
<b>Results depend only on effort. </b>
<b>And effort depends on your focus.</b>

155
00:10:58.041 --> 00:11:00.958
<b>If your ambitions are high,</b>

156
00:11:00.958 --> 00:11:03.666
<b>consider this,</b>

157
00:11:03.666 --> 00:11:07.083
<b>if you have achieved a high goal,</b>

158
00:11:07.083 --> 00:11:09.375
<b>have made a plan for it,</b>

159
00:11:09.375 --> 00:11:14.541
<b> then now it would be appropriate </b>
<b>that your attention should be on the actions,</b>

160
00:11:14.541 --> 00:11:19.166
<b>on every step that will take you to the goal.</b>

161
00:11:19.166 --> 00:11:23.125
<b>If you keep looking only at the goal while walking,</b>

162
00:11:23.125 --> 00:11:25.583
<b>but the attention is diverted from the path,</b>

163
00:11:25.583 --> 00:11:30.416
<b>you may stumble and fall somewhere.</b>

164
00:11:30.416 --> 00:11:36.916
<b>Despite being ambitious, not being attached </b>
<b>to the result means</b>

165
00:11:36.916 --> 00:11:41.833
<b>that you are completely absorbed in your work,</b>

166
00:11:41.833 --> 00:11:47.541
<b>you are constantly trying to</b>
<b>increase the level of your work,</b>

167
00:11:47.541 --> 00:11:50.958
<b>and there is progress in your personality.</b>

168
00:11:50.958 --> 00:11:55.416
<b>Whatever the result may be, </b>
<b>it makes no difference.</b>

169
00:11:55.416 --> 00:11:59.083
<b>If the result is good, you keep working;</b>

170
00:11:59.083 --> 00:12:03.416
<b>if it is bad, you learn from it and move forward.</b>

171
00:12:03.416 --> 00:12:04.666
<b>Think about it,</b>

172
00:12:04.666 --> 00:12:08.250
<b>if you start enjoying the journey itself,</b>

173
00:12:08.250 --> 00:12:11.250
<b>will the worry of the destination bother you?</b>

174
00:12:11.250 --> 00:12:16.083
<b>Won't the destination itself come walking to you?</b>

175
00:12:16.083 --> 00:12:22.375
<b>Working without worrying about </b>
<b>the result is just like that.</b>

176
00:12:22.375 --> 00:12:24.166
<b>Think about this.</b>

